instruction:
Briefly describe what you see and hear in this clip, using only actual evidence. Then assess it. The intended scene is two straight punches into the heavy bag, return to guard after each, then one step back and stop. Intended sound is plausible impacts and gym ambience, without speech or music. The intended scene is NOT evidence that these events happened. Do not infer audible sounds from visible actions.

Return one flat JSON object, no prose outside it. Use exactly these keys:
"observed_video": a brief description of actual action and appearance;
"observed_audio": a brief description of actual sound, or silence;
"audible_sound": true, false, or null;
"speech_present": true, false, or null;
"music_present": true, false, or null;
"action_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"temporal_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"appearance_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"audio_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"synchronization_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"overall_score": integer 0..4 or null;
"sync_evidence": a short explanation of whether audible events match visible contacts, with uncertainty when timing cannot be resolved;
"uncertainty": a short explanation of any limitations.

Scale: 0 fails badly, 1 major faults, 2 mixed, 3 good with minor faults, 4 convincing. Action measures intended order/contact/ending; temporal measures stable anatomy and motion; appearance measures coherent subjects/texture/lighting; audio measures plausible sounds without unwanted speech/music; synchronization measures audiovisual contact timing; overall is a preference, not a calculated average. Video is sparsely sampled. Use null when a dimension cannot be assessed. Do not assign a perfect synchronization score to silence. Keep every text field to one short sentence.
